    "text": {
     "en": "Acids taste sour and bases feel soapy. Lemon, vinegar and curd have acids. Soap and baking soda are bases.\nWhen an acid and a base mix they cancel each other's effect. This is neutralisation and it gives salt and water.\nAn antacid tablet is a base that neutralises extra acid in the stomach. Ant stings have acid, so we apply baking soda."
    }
